id: shock-collar
name: Shock Collar
kind: gear
itemType: accessory
tags: tech
craftDC: Expert
# "This Accessory is connected to a Remote Control." Paired when it is given, so the Remote
# Control finds it on whoever ends up wearing it.
paired: true
# "Reduce your Life Points by 1/5 of your Maximum Life Points. If you are knocked through a
# Health Threshold by this effect, you are knocked Prone."
shockPart: 5
shockProne: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Set off from its Remote Control: 1/5 of the wearer's Maximum Life Points, and Prone if that
  knocks them through a Health Threshold.
text: >
  Shock Collar [Tech]: This collar is designed to emit an electric shock when the
  corresponding remote is triggered.
  –Craft DC: Expert
  –Effects: This Accessory is connected to a Remote Control. If the Remote Control triggers
  the effects of a Shock Collar, reduce your Life Points by 1/5 of your Maximum Life Points.
  If you are knocked through a Health Threshold by this effect, you are knocked Prone.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Given: paired, so a Remote Control connected to it finds it wherever it is worn.
#
# A Remote Control's row names it, and whom it is on; Trigger, for the Remote's Action, takes
# 1/5 of the wearer's Maximum Life Points - a Life Point reduction, past Soak and Damage
# Reduction, rounded down - and knocks them Prone if that knocked them through a Health
# Threshold. Only while it is worn.
#
# --- What the table keeps ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Getting it onto somebody: the entry does not say how, so it is the table's - drag it to
# their sheet and they put it on. It keeps its pair wherever it goes.
